# n8n PPC Negatives Diff Workflow

## Overview
This n8n workflow automatically updates the `Negatives_Diff` sheet in your "PPC- Negative Keyword Lists" Google Spreadsheet by comparing negative keywords between Google Ads (GA) and Microsoft Ads (MS) platforms.

## Workflow File
The workflow is defined in: `ppc-negatives-diff-workflow.json`

## What This Workflow Does

### Data Sources
1. **GA_Negatives** tab - Auto-updated daily from Google Ads platform
2. **MS_Negatives** tab - Manually updated
3. **Negatives_Diff** tab - Auto-updated by this workflow

### Logic

#### Finding Keywords to Add to MS (add_to_MS column)
- Looks at specific list_names in GA_Negatives:
  - bad tech
  - PC, invest, sensitive content, sites, logins, misc
  - skill-seekers, deals, errors
  - too short
  - competitors
  - too short - sql perf
  - SQL Deployments
  - Irrelevant info queries
- Compares these keywords with MS_Negatives
- If a keyword is NOT in MS_Negatives, it gets added to the add_to_MS column
- **Important**: Match types matter - "sql server" (phrase) and [sql server] (exact) are treated as different keywords

#### Finding Keywords to Add to GA (add_to_GA column)
- Looks at all keywords in MS_Negatives
- Compares with GA_Negatives
- If a keyword is NOT in GA_Negatives, it gets added to the add_to_GA column

## Setup Instructions

### 1. Import the Workflow into n8n
1. Open your n8n instance
2. Click on "Workflows" in the left sidebar
3. Click the "Import from File" button
4. Select the `ppc-negatives-diff-workflow.json` file
5. The workflow will be imported with all nodes configured

### 2. Configure Google Sheets Credentials
1. In n8n, go to "Credentials" in the left sidebar
2. Click "Add Credential"
3. Select "Google Sheets OAuth2 API"
4. Follow the authentication flow to connect your Google account
5. Note the credential ID (you'll need this in the next step)

### 3. Update the Workflow Parameters
Open the workflow and update the following in each Google Sheets node:

**In all Google Sheets nodes:**
- Replace `YOUR_SPREADSHEET_ID` with your actual Google Spreadsheet ID
  - You can find this in the URL: `https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/SPREADSHEET_ID/edit`
- Replace `YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEETS_CREDENTIAL_ID` with the credential ID from step 2

**Google Sheets nodes to update:**
- Read GA_Negatives
- Read MS_Negatives
- Clear Negatives_Diff
- Write to Negatives_Diff

### 4. Configure the Schedule (Optional)
The workflow is set to run every 24 hours by default. To change this:
1. Click on the "Schedule Trigger" node
2. Adjust the interval as needed (e.g., every 12 hours, daily at specific time, etc.)

Alternatively, you can replace the Schedule Trigger with a Manual Trigger if you want to run it on-demand only.

### 5. Activate the Workflow
1. Click the "Activate" toggle in the top right corner
2. The workflow will now run automatically based on your schedule

## Testing the Workflow

Before activating, you should test the workflow:
1. Click "Execute Workflow" button to run it manually
2. Check each node to see the data flow
3. Verify the Negatives_Diff sheet is updated correctly
4. Confirm that the logic matches your expectations

## Workflow Structure

```
Schedule Trigger (runs every 24 hours)
    ↓
    ├→ Read GA_Negatives (reads all data from GA_Negatives tab)
    |       ↓
    └→ Read MS_Negatives (reads all data from MS_Negatives tab)
            ↓
    Process Differences (JavaScript code to compare and find differences)
            ↓
    Clear Negatives_Diff (clears existing data in Negatives_Diff tab)
            ↓
    Write to Negatives_Diff (writes new comparison results)
```

## Output Format

The Negatives_Diff sheet will have two columns:

| add_to_GA | add_to_MS |
|-----------|-----------|
| keyword1 (match_type) | keyword2 (match_type) |
| keyword3 (match_type) | keyword4 (match_type) |

Example:
| add_to_GA | add_to_MS |
|-----------|-----------|
| sql training (phrase) | python tutorial (exact) |
| database admin (exact) | server management (phrase) |

## Troubleshooting

### Workflow Fails to Read Sheets
- Check that Google Sheets credentials are properly configured
- Verify the spreadsheet ID is correct
- Ensure the sheet tab names match exactly: GA_Negatives, MS_Negatives, Negatives_Diff

### No Data in Output
- Verify that GA_Negatives and MS_Negatives have data
- Check that column names match: list_name, keyword, match_type, first_seen_at, last_synced_at, is_new
- Review the "Process Differences" node output to see intermediate results

### Incorrect Matches
- Ensure match types are consistent in your data
- Remember that match types are case-sensitive in the comparison
- Verify that the list_name values in GA_Negatives exactly match the target list names

## Maintenance

- The workflow will run automatically based on your schedule
- Monitor execution history in n8n to ensure it's running successfully
- If you add new list_names to track, update the `targetListNames` array in the "Process Differences" Code node

## Notes

- The workflow clears and rewrites the entire Negatives_Diff sheet each time it runs
- Make sure GA_Negatives is being updated from Google Ads before this workflow runs
- The workflow preserves match type distinctions (phrase vs exact vs broad)
